exit: 2
--- stdout
--- stderr
usage: riftc <command> [options] [file]

commands:
  lex <file>            print the token stream of a .rifts/.rifth file
  parse <file>          print the syntax tree of one file
  check <file>          check a module and everything it imports
  symbols <file>        print the module's merged symbol table (header + source)
  typed <file>          print the syntax tree with the type of every expression
  build <file>          compile a program to build/<mode>/<name> (next to the file)
  build [targets]       build the programs of ./build.rifts (or the targets named)
  run <file> [-- args]  build a program in a temporary directory and run it
  run <target>          build and run a program of ./build.rifts
  test [tests]          build and run the tests of ./build.rifts
  emit-llvm <file>      print the LLVM IR the program compiles to
  insights <file>       list what the compiler does implicitly (stack, heap, drops, moves, ...) as JSON
  expand <file> <type>  print a type with the members its annotations generate written out
  explain [code|id]     describe a diagnostic code or a warning id, or list all codes

options:
  --diagnostic-format=human|short   diagnostic layout (default: human)
  --color=auto|always|never         colored diagnostics (default: auto)
  --root=DIR                        project root for imports and build.rifts (default: the file's
                                    directory; for build.rifts the current directory)
  --stop-after=PHASE                lex, parse, resolve, types or ownership
  --mode=MODE                       debug (default), release, release_with_debug_info, or a mode
                                    of build.rifts
  --warn=ID=off|error|on            switch a warning of a check, e.g. --warn=gfx::deprecated=off
  -o FILE, --output=FILE            where 'build' writes the executable
  -DNAME=VALUE                      an option of build.rifts
  --list                            build: list build.rifts' targets, modes and options
  --compile-commands                build: write compile_commands.json for the C/C++ targets
  --out-dir=DIR                     where a build.rifts build goes (default: <root>/build)
  --bin-dir=DIR                     where a build.rifts build puts its programs (default: <out-dir>/<mode>)
  --cc=COMPILER                     linker for build/run (default: $RIFT_CC, else cc)
  --target=PLATFORM                 build for another platform: x86_64-linux-gnu, aarch64-linux-gnu,
                                    riscv64-linux-gnu (links with PLATFORM-gcc, else clang --target)
  --all-functions                   generate every function, not only those main reaches (testing)
  -h, --help                        show this help
  -V, --version                     show the compiler version

exit codes: 0 success, 1 errors in input, 2 bad command line, 3 internal error;
            'run' exits with the program's own status (128 + signal if it crashed)
